2026-09-30 04:50 Build: make TARGET=android-armv7 builds all 19 test binaries after 3 build fixes: (1) src/net/dns.c used IPPROTO_TCP via netdb.h only (bionic needs <netinet/in.h>); (2) dns.c ai_addrlen > sizeof compare warns under clang/bionic where socklen_t is signed int; (3) Lua's default lua_getlocaledecpoint() calls localeconv(), absent from bionic before API 21 -> configured by flag in mk/lua.mk for android only. NDK has no libpthread: -lpthread routed through PTHREAD_LIBS. Runner: tools/android-test.sh via make TARGET=android-armv7 test-device. Device run next.

2026-09-30 05:08 Device run 1 (A7600-H, before TLS fix): 16/19 pass; test_llm_http, test_loop_native, http_test fail+timeout, all via TLS to the forked tsrv. Root cause: Mbed TLS only uses getrandom() under __GLIBC__; on bionic (and musl) it reads MBEDTLS_PLATFORM_DEV_RANDOM, default /dev/random, which blocks on kernel 3.4 while entropy_avail < read_wakeup_threshold (57 < 64 on the idle tablet). wchan of both the test process (client DRBG seed = owner thread in the runtime) and the tsrv child = random_read. Contradicts HTTP transport spec §5 ('getrandom()/ /dev/urandom'). Fix: MBEDTLS_PLATFORM_DEV_RANDOM "/dev/urandom" in src/net/canlin_mbedtls_config.h + regression check test_entropy_source in t/net/http_test.c (red on host before the fix). A/B on device with entropy drained by a background /dev/random reader: pre-fix binary blocks in random_read, fixed binaries pass.

2026-09-30 05:08 Device run 2: 18/19 pass. Remaining: t/net/http_test.c:705/708/767 (connect-stall and connect-cancel via full accept queue of tsrv's listen(fd,0) backlog listener). Cause: Linux 3.4 tcp_v4_conn_request drops a SYN on a full accept queue only when >1 young request is in the SYN queue, so the client still gets SYN-ACK and reaches ESTABLISHED (device /proc/net/tcp: pre-connect client 01 while server side 03 SYN_RECV). Newer kernels drop the SYN outright. Test-fixture portability, not a transport bug; not fixed here -> card proposal (test-writer lane).

